WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:11.380
We have to be clear: the world has never been
better than it is right now.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:16.900
Thanks mostly to globalization there are less
and less wars, global poverty is falling markedly

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:20.230
and quality of life is generally improving.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:25.820
This is obviously not happening in a uniform
way across all countries, but it is true from

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:26.820
a global perspective.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.680
However, and against all odds, many western
countries have decided to rebel and refuse

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.860
openness and understanding among their nations.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.180
In Europe, for example, extreme right-wing
parties are spreading uncertainty: Le Pen

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:46.640
in France, Wilders in the Netherlands, and
Hofer in Austria are good examples of this

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.530
new wave which has also reached countries
like Finland, Denmark, Germany and Hungary,

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:52.530
among others.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:01:03.199
Further, it has also been partly responsible
for the Brexit victory in the United Kingdom.

00:01:03.199 --> 00:01:07.420
It is a movement which is taking advantage
of fear, despite the fact that we are living

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.060
in societies which are becoming safer and
safer.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:13.659
But, as you all know, these ideas are not
exclusive to Europe.

00:01:13.659 --> 00:01:18.570
Donald Trump won the US election and has spoken
about his views which are clearly contrary

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:20.920
to globalisation and immigration.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:25.820
At this point the best question we can ask
is: Are there any developed countries left

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:30.460
who still believe in open borders and globalisation?

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:32.869
Well, there are.

00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:38.840
And today we are going to look at one of the
most significant of these countries.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.860
-CANADA’S OPENNESS-

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:49.509
In the year 2016, Canada has admitted into
their country more than 300,000 new immigrants.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:53.679
That is close 1% of its total population.

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:56.990
This is a greater proportion than any other
large developed country

00:01:56.990 --> 00:02:00.049
And note here that this is not something that
is new, the measure has been in force for

00:02:00.049 --> 00:02:01.159
more than two decades.

00:02:01.159 --> 00:02:07.320
The result of this, today, one in every five
Canadians was born abroad, a percentage which

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.100
is almost double that of the US or the UK.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:21.290
And, truth be told, this hasn’t led to any
national tragedy, in fact, quite the contrary.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:22.970
And Canadians are the first to know this.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:28.490
According to the prestigious Environics Institute,
most citizens (almost 80% of them) consider

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:33.290
immigration to be good for the economy and
that it represents the best way to deal with

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:44.349
important issues such as it ageing population.

00:02:44.349 --> 00:02:47.180
If you think about it, this does make sense:

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:51.739
Employment is the country's most productive
asset, so, why should they prevent it from

00:02:51.739 --> 00:02:52.739
growing?

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:55.959
In the context of a dynamic economy, what’s
the harm of immigrants who are willing to

00:02:55.959 --> 00:02:59.319
work, set up companies, or get an education?

00:02:59.319 --> 00:03:05.569
It is, we think, something good.

00:03:05.569 --> 00:03:09.440
-TRUDEAU’S FIRST YEAR-

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:14.299
In October 2015, Justin Trudeau became Canada’s
Prime Minister after defeating, against all

00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:18.829
odds, the conservative Stephen Harper, who
had held office for almost ten years.

00:03:18.829 --> 00:03:23.720
Since then, the political agenda has been
dominated by a determination to deepen the

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.030
country’s pro-globalisation policies.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:29.959
Trudeau himself, a left-winger, has become
quite an advocate of promoting free trade

00:03:29.959 --> 00:03:31.340
and social mobility.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:34.909
In his first year in office he signed a free
trade agreement with the European Union and

00:03:34.909 --> 00:03:37.470
confirmed Canada’s adherence to TPP.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:42.360
Although Trump’s first action was to destroy
it, it was meant to be the biggest commercial

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.849
agreement in history.

00:03:43.849 --> 00:03:48.890
In just a year Canada built up free trade
relationships with almost 60% of world’s

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:49.890
economy.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:59.260
And Trudeau wants to expand this further,
and increase trade with China.

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:03.469
And the government is doing more of the same
concerning immigration.

00:04:03.469 --> 00:04:19.940
They have even set the goal of increasing
the number of immigrants they receive by 50%

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.210
every year.

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:26.200
Given these principles, it shouldn’t surprise
you to hear that Canada is one of the most

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.820
committed countries when making things easy
for Syrian refugees.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:34.220
Canada has received more than 33,000 Syrians
since Trudeau became Prime Minister.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:42.100
In his first year, Trudeau himself personally
went to Toronto’s airport to welcome them

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:47.130
into the country.

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.690
-MIGRATION POLICY-

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.260
But wait!

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:53.130
Immigration in Canada is not free.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.040
It’s more regulated than we at VisualPolitik,
would like.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:59.630
But, what is important here, is not whether
there are, or are not, excessive administrative

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:03.540
requirements, but that citizens shouldn’t
automatically view as criminals those who

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:05.950
come to work or live in other countries.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:10.290
And this is precisely why Canada is quite
so successful - they are a country which takes

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:15.260
pride in looking for additional citizens,
not temporary immigrants.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:21.410
Since 1967, admission has been based on a
points system which considers qualification,

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:25.730
experience, professional skills, or knowledge
of English or French.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:35.370
In the same way, this system also gives priority
to those professionals needed by companies.

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:46.970
The 
tendency seems to be to make these procedures

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:47.970
easier.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:53.530
But what is important is the social recognition
and the integration of immigrants into the

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:54.530
country.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:58.580
The Canadian Bill of Rights itself recognizes
the concept of multicultural patrimony.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:02.670
There are solid policies to encourage integration
which, by the way, usually encourage the newcomers

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:10.100
not to lose their own cultural identity and
consider diversity an enriching factor.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:19.650
For example, in Canadian schools, it is easy
to find classes taught in Spanish or Ukrainian.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:24.440
The results support these policies indeed:
in the last decade, Canada’s growth has

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:30.971
been bigger than the US, Germany or the UK,
and a high standard of living exists in the

00:06:30.971 --> 00:06:31.971
country.

00:06:31.971 --> 00:06:34.430
Now it might be easier to understand why Canada’s
immigration website collapsed few hours after

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:37.640
Trump’s victory was known.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:44.950
Or why there were front covers of the Economist
highlighting Canada’s liberty.

00:06:44.950 --> 00:06:49.330
Of course Canada´s model isn’t perfect.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:53.970
But compared to the new nationalist and populist
tendencies of other countries, Canada shows

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:57.780
how desirable openness alternative really
is.

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:04.130
The key takeaway here is to try to make things
better instead of isolating your country from

00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:07.770
the rest of the world - the latter of which
is an argument that other politicians like

00:07:07.770 --> 00:07:10.310
Trump are defending.

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:16.240
Well, now it’s your turn: Do you think immigration
generates as many problems as some claim?

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:19.520
Would you rather live in an open and diverse
society like Canada?

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:25.360
We will be waiting for your answers and, please,
if you haven’t yet subscribed to VisualPolitik,

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:27.720
you can do so by clicking the logo on the
screen now!

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:29.390
We´d also ask you to click the “like”
button if you enjoyed this alternative to

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:30.390
some of Trump’s policies.

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:31.970
And as always, I’ll see you in the next
video!

